From c7820b328f7aa0744cec1e2bc43c4c65b5204bc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:53:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add the CellBroadcast interface on top of oFono's
 CellBroadcast

Phosh shows warnings (EU-Alert/DE-Alert, ETWS) as a full-screen prompt
and cellbroadcastd stores them, but both read them from ModemManager's
org.freedesktop.ModemManager1.Modem.CellBroadcast, which oFono2MM did not
offer: oFono received the messages and nobody showed them. cellbroadcastd
could not set the channel list either.

Export the interface for every modem:
- SetChannels/Channels map to oFono's "Topics" (oFono stores them per SIM
  and adds the ETWS channels itself). oFono offers CellBroadcast only once
  the SIM is ready, so a list set before is applied then.
- Every message oFono reports (IncomingBroadcastWithProperties,
  IncomingBroadcast, EmergencyBroadcast) becomes a complete CBM object
  with text, channel, message code and update number. oFono sends the
  first two for the same message; only one CBM is created.
- Nothing on a phone deletes CBMs and the network repeats alerts, so
  only the latest 50 are kept.
